"*":{"decision":"47","why":"Decision 47 (bug 22): `importsCandidates` answers `{found: false}` when there is no file, `{found: true, unreadable: <message>}` when it can't be read or doesn't parse (`<message>` is any non-empty text naming no path), and otherwise `{found: true, candidates}`, today's list in today's order (unsupported drivers still left out): each candidate has `key` (TablePlus: `id:<ID>`, the entry's `ID` as text with an `id:` prefix, or `pos:<n>` for an entry keyed by its 0-based position in the list; DBeaver: the connection's key in `connections`, as it is), today's `name`, `type`, `host`, `port`, `databaseName`, `username`, `sslMode` and `sshTunnel`, `duplicateOf` (the id of the project's connection with the same type, host, port, database and user) in place of `isDuplicate` and `selected`, and `problem: \"invalidPort\"` with `port: 0` for a port that isn't a number (today `NaN`, recorded as \"NaN\") or is outside 0–65535 (`-1`, `65536`, `70000`). Other ports follow `parseInt` (leading digits). TablePlus entries are every dict in the list: one with no `ID` gets `key: \"pos:<n>\"` and `problem: \"noId\"` (today it's dropped), and entries sharing an `ID` each get `pos:<n>` and `problem: \"duplicateId\"`. The prefixes keep the two kinds of key apart: no `ID` can make an `id:` key equal a `pos:` one; those problems come before `invalidPort`. After the Task 4a review (coordinator's decision): `problem: \"invalidSshPort\"`, with the tunnel's `port: 0`, for a TablePlus SSH port outside 0–65535 (`parseInt` keeps `-5` or `70000`), and `problem: \"noName\"` for a DBeaver connection whose name is missing, `null` or blank, since `connectionCreate` refuses both; they come after `invalidPort`. No recorded case has either shape, so `tests/imports_plan.rs` pins them and no case's `expected` changes. `importsCreate` refuses a key whose candidate has a `problem` (`INVALID_ARGUMENT`, naming the key), whatever the GUI sends.","expected":{}},
